      "ar": "`WITH paid AS (SELECT ...) SELECT ... FROM paid` بيقسّم استعلام طويل لخطوات بأسماء — أوضح بكتير من استعلامات جوه بعض. والتواريخ في SQLite نصوص ISO (`2026-09-30`)، فبتتقارن وتترتب صح، و`strftime('%Y-%m', day)` بيطلّع الشهر للتجميع، و`date('now', '-30 days')` من 30 يوم.",
      "en": "`WITH paid AS (SELECT ...) SELECT ... FROM paid` splits a long query into named steps — much clearer than queries nested in each other. Dates in SQLite are ISO strings (`2026-09-30`), so they compare and sort correctly; `strftime('%Y-%m', day)` extracts the month for grouping, and `date('now', '-30 days')` is 30 days ago."
