     "p": {
      "ar": "اقرا CSV بـ DictReader، ونضّف (أسبوع 10 و11)، وادخّله بـ executemany في transaction، واعمل upsert لو هتعيد التحميل كل يوم. وبعد كده أي تقرير = استعلام SQL واحد بدل لوبات Python. وطلّع النتيجة CSV أو Excel منسّق أو JSON للوحة (أسبوع 15).",
      "en": "Read the CSV with DictReader, clean it (weeks 10 and 11), insert it with executemany inside a transaction, and upsert when reloading daily. After that, any report is one SQL query instead of Python loops. Export the result as CSV, a formatted Excel file or JSON for the dashboard (week 15)."
     },
     "ex": "import csv, io, sqlite3\ncsv_text = \"day,city,product,qty,price\\n2026-09-01,Cairo,Pen,10,7.5\\n2026-09-01,Giza,Bag,1,650\\n2026-09-02,Cairo,Bag,2,650\\n2026-09-02,Alex,Notebook,5,45\\n\"\ndb = sqlite3.connect(\":memory:\")\ndb.execute(\"CREATE TABLE sales (day TEXT, city TEXT, product TEXT, qty INTEGER, price REAL)\")\nrows = [(r[\"day\"], r[\"city\"], r[\"product\"], int(r[\"qty\"]), float(r[\"price\"])) for r in csv.DictReader(io.StringIO(csv_text))]\nwith db:\n    db.executemany(\"INSERT INTO sales VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?)\", rows)\nreport = db.execute(\"SELECT city, SUM(qty * price) AS revenue FROM sales GROUP BY city ORDER BY revenue DESC\").fetchall()\nout = io.StringIO()\nw = csv.writer(out)\nw.writerow([\"city\", \"revenue\"]); w.writerows(report)\nprint(out.getvalue())",
